      "side": 1,
      "message": "looks like this parse() is dup to NetlinkMessage.parse(). Instead of duplicating the code, how about just adding the corresponding family in the NetlinkMessage.parse, something like:\n```\n        // Netlink family messages. The netlink family is required. Note that the reason for using\n        // if-statement is that switch-case can\u0027t be used because the OsConstants.NETLINK_* are\n        // not constant.\n        final NetlinkMessage parsed;\n        if (nlFamily \u003d\u003d OsConstants.NETLINK_ROUTE) {\n            parsed \u003d parseRtMessage(nlmsghdr, byteBuffer);\n        } else if (nlFamily \u003d\u003d OsConstants.NETLINK_INET_DIAG) {\n            parsed \u003d parseInetDiagMessage(nlmsghdr, byteBuffer);\n        } else if (nlFamily \u003d\u003d OsConstants.NETLINK_NETFILTER) {\n            parsed \u003d parseNfMessage(nlmsghdr, byteBuffer);\n        } else if (nlFamily \u003d\u003d OsConstants.NETLINK_XFRM) { // assume that NETLINK_XFRM is the correct family type.\n            parsed \u003d parseXfrmMessage(nlmsghdr, byteBuffer);\n        } else {\n            parsed \u003d null;\n        }\n```\n\nThen in parseXfrmMessage(), we can do something similar to the rtnetlink:\n```\n    @Nullable\n    private static NetlinkMessage parseXfrmMessage(@NonNull StructNlMsgHdr nlmsghdr,\n            @NonNull ByteBuffer byteBuffer) {\n        switch (nlmsghdr.nlmsg_type) {\n            case NetlinkConstants.XFRM_MSG_GETSA:\n                return (NetlinkMessage) IpSecXfrmNetlinkGetSaMessage.parse(nlmsghdr, byteBuffer);\n            // TODO: support other XFRM_* relevant message type.\n            default: return null;\n        }\n    }\n```\n\nThen I guess probably we don\u0027t need a separate IpSecXfrmNetlinkMessage class? given the xfrmnetlink message is still a netlink message, the header should be identical, is it? If so, then we can just use NetlinkMessage class.",
